---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Methodology | HUMANITY"
  description="How HUMANITY collects source reports, structures candidate events, assesses evidence, and controls publication."
>
  <main class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-4 py-12 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <header class="max-w-3xl border-b border-humanity-border pb-9">
      <p class="eyebrow">Evidence, provenance, limits</p>
      <h1 class="editorial-title mt-3 text-4xl font-semibold sm:text-6xl">
        How the record is made.
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-humanity-textMuted">
        HUMANITY turns reports from configured sources into candidate event
        records. Automation can organize evidence; it cannot establish that a
        report is true or make the source mix complete.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section
      class="grid gap-0 border-b border-humanity-border py-8 md:grid-cols-2"
      aria-label="Method principles"
    >
      <article class="border-b border-humanity-border py-5 md:border-r md:pr-8">
        <p class="eyebrow">01 · Provenance</p>
        <h2 class="editorial-title mt-2 text-2xl font-semibold">
          Claims point back to reporting.
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-humanity-textMuted">
          An extraction is a candidate, not a source. Public records retain
          source links and claim attribution so a reader can inspect the
          original reporting.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="border-b border-humanity-border py-5 md:pl-8">
        <p class="eyebrow">02 · Independence</p>
        <h2 class="editorial-title mt-2 text-2xl font-semibold">
          Copies do not make corroboration.
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-humanity-textMuted">
          The pipeline checks for shared wire attribution and copied content.
          Suspected syndication is not treated as independent confirmation; one
          article can support extraction but cannot satisfy independent-source
          corroboration by itself.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="border-b border-humanity-border py-5 md:border-r md:pr-8">
        <p class="eyebrow">03 · Uncertainty</p>
        <h2 class="editorial-title mt-2 text-2xl font-semibold">
          Disagreement stays visible.
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-humanity-textMuted">
          Claims may be reported, corroborated, disputed, or uncertain.
          Conflicts and weak evidence can hold a candidate out of public feeds
          rather than be resolved by guessing.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="border-b border-humanity-border py-5 md:pl-8">
        <p class="eyebrow">04 · Restraint</p>
        <h2 class="editorial-title mt-2 text-2xl font-semibold">
          No threshold is lowered to fill a page.
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-humanity-textMuted">
          An empty feed is preferable to an unsupported publication. Extraction
          success, model confidence, and story importance do not independently
          qualify an event for publication.
        </p>
      </article>
    </section>

    <section class="py-9" aria-labelledby="pipeline-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">The processing path</p>
      <h2
        id="pipeline-heading"
        class="editorial-title mt-2 text-3xl font-semibold"
      >
        From configured source to public record
      </h2>
      <ol
        class="mt-6 divide-y divide-humanity-border border-y border-humanity-border"
      >
        <li class="grid gap-2 py-5 sm:grid-cols-[3rem_1fr]">
          <span class="font-mono text-sm text-humanity-accent">01</span><div>
            <h3 class="font-semibold">Discover and retain source records</h3><p
              class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-humanity-textMuted"
            >
              The configured registry includes news, RSS/API, data-provider, and
              institutional sources. Adapters normalize reporting metadata and
              may retrieve article text for extraction. A configured source is
              not proof that it was successfully contacted or that its terms
              have been reviewed.
            </p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="grid gap-2 py-5 sm:grid-cols-[3rem_1fr]">
          <span class="font-mono text-sm text-humanity-accent">02</span><div>
            <h3 class="font-semibold">Extract candidate facts</h3><p
              class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-humanity-textMuted"
            >
              When a provider is available and a call budget permits, Gemini
              returns structured candidate information that is schema-validated.
              Quota, network, or provider failures may defer work. Model output
              is not treated as independent evidence.
            </p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="grid gap-2 py-5 sm:grid-cols-[3rem_1fr]">
          <span class="font-mono text-sm text-humanity-accent">03</span><div>
            <h3 class="font-semibold">Deduplicate cautiously</h3><p
              class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-humanity-textMuted"
            >
              Canonical source URLs and stored identifiers help make source
              ingestion idempotent. Separate reporting about the same occurrence
              may be matched conservatively; ambiguous or nearby events should
              remain separate rather than be force-merged.
            </p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="grid gap-2 py-5 sm:grid-cols-[3rem_1fr]">
          <span class="font-mono text-sm text-humanity-accent">04</span><div>
            <h3 class="font-semibold">
              Assess evidence and publication readiness
            </h3><p
              class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-humanity-textMuted"
            >
              Source independence, syndication, claim support, contradictions,
              confidence, and configured policy thresholds are evaluated
              separately from extraction. HELD and REJECTED records are excluded
              from public artifacts.
            </p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="grid gap-2 py-5 sm:grid-cols-[3rem_1fr]">
          <span class="font-mono text-sm text-humanity-accent">05</span><div>
            <h3 class="font-semibold">Build static public pages and feeds</h3><p
              class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-humanity-textMuted"
            >
              Only records admitted by publication policy are included in public
              event feeds and derived pages. Browser refreshes reload the last
              generated data; they do not run the source-ingestion pipeline.
            </p>
          </div>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section
      class="grid gap-8 border-y border-humanity-border py-9 md:grid-cols-2"
    >
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">What is not promised</p>
        <h2 class="editorial-title mt-2 text-3xl font-semibold">
          Coverage is partial.
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-humanity-textMuted">
          Sources vary in geography, language, access, and update cadence. The
          project has no measured completeness denominator and cannot reliably
          represent every event or affected person. Dates, locations, and impact
          numbers can be incomplete or revised.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Current engineering limits</p>
        <h2 class="editorial-title mt-2 text-3xl font-semibold">
          Some handoffs remain unfinished.
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-humanity-textMuted">
          The source-identity and event-resolution components exist, but the
          command-line ingestion path has not yet been verified to route every
          extracted event through the full clusterer. Automated publication is
          disabled by default, and production release and recurring ingestion
          require explicit gates.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="grid gap-8 py-9 md:grid-cols-2">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Provider reliability</p>
        <h2 class="editorial-title mt-2 text-3xl font-semibold">
          A successful call is not verification.
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-humanity-textMuted">
          The Gemini integration uses the supported Google Gen AI SDK with
          bounded calls and credential-slot rotation. The latest recorded
          real-source tests encountered provider-side server errors; these
          diagnostics do not establish a permanent provider cause. No real API
          call is needed to verify deterministic application behavior.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Content rights</p>
        <h2 class="editorial-title mt-2 text-3xl font-semibold">
          Attribution is not permission.
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-humanity-textMuted">
          Fetched text can be persisted for processing, while public pages link
          to reporting and may display short attributed excerpts.
          Source-specific storage, quotation, commercial-use, and redistribution
          rights remain under review. No commercial reuse is cleared.
        </p>
        <a href="/source-rights" class="link mt-4 inline-block"
          >Read source-rights and reuse status →</a
        >
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="border-t border-humanity-border pt-8">
      <h2 class="editorial-title text-2xl font-semibold">
        Review the implementation
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-3 max-w-3xl leading-relaxed text-humanity-textMuted">
        The code, source configuration, scoring policy, and issue history are
        public. Read the <a href="/sources" class="link"
          >configured source registry</a
        >, the <a href="/source-rights" class="link">rights register</a>, and <a
          href="https://github.com/asdfhgds/humanity"
          class="link"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer">the project repository ↗</a
        >. Report a correction through the public <a
          href="https://github.com/asdfhgds/humanity/issues"
          class="link"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer">issue tracker ↗</a
        >; avoid posting sensitive personal information.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
